"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.10690561551986529,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.47726734548898886,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.01911,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":12.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"SoundHound AI, Inc. provides independent voice artificial intelligence (AI) solutions that enables businesses across the automotive, TV, IoT, and customer service industries to deliver conversational experiences to customers in the United States, Korea, France, Japan, Germany, and internationally. The company offers Houndify platform, which provides a suite of Houndify tools to help brands build conversational voice assistants, such as Application Programming Interfaces (API) for text and voice queries, support for custom commands, extensive library of content domains, inclusive software development kit platforms, collaboration capabilities, diagnostic tools, and built-in analytics; SoundHound Chat AI, a voice assistant with integrated generative AI that integrates with knowledge domains, pulling real-time data, such as weather, sports, stocks, flight status, restaurants, and other data; and SoundHound Smart Answering, which offers customer establishments the option to build an easy to use custom AI-powered voice assistant. It also provides CaiNET software that uses machine learning to enhance how domains work together to handle complex queries; CaiLAN software that arbitrates responses, so users get answers from the right domain; Dynamic Interaction, a real-time multimodal customer service interface; Smart Ordering, which offers an easy-to-understand voice assistant for restaurants; automatic speech recognition; natural language understanding; wake words; custom domains; text-to-speech; Employee Assist; and edge and cloud connectivity, which includes embedded voice solutions. In addition, the company offers Amelia Platform, which builds AI agents for enterprises; Chat AI for Automotive; Dynamic Drive-Thru for GenAI; Voice Commerce, which connects drivers and merchants with Voice AI; Autonomics Platform; Custom Voice AI Solutions; Voice AI Platform; and SoundHound Music App. SoundHound AI, Inc. was founded in 2005 and is headquartered in Santa Clara, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Keyvan  Mohajer | Co-Founder, CEO, President & Director | Age 47 | Compensation: $546,333 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 954 people. Revenue per employee of $177K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, improving at 76%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $85K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["SoundHound AI, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $1.8B market cap on $169M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +76% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -205% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $99M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +12.2% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -34.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 48% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +12.2% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (41.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 21% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 69/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 172% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"SoundHound AI (SOUN) Q3 Results Reveal A Margin Squeeze","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nasdaq-soun/soundhound-ai/news/soundhound-ai-soun-q3-results-reveal-a-margin-squeeze","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794011746.757,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.69,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why SoundHound AI (SOUN) stock is down today","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nasdaq/soun/news/why-up-down/why-soundhound-ai-soun-stock-is-down-today-2","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793998236.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is SoundHound AI (SOUN) Above Fair Value After New Deals?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nasdaq-soun/soundhound-ai/news/is-soundhound-ai-soun-above-fair-value-after-new-deals","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793996906.823,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.97,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SOUN Plunges 22.8% in the Past Month. Is the Sell-Off an Opportunity?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025871/soun-plunges-22-8-in-the-past-month-is-the-sell-off-an-opportunity?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog_plus%7Czer_report_insights-3025871","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793984220.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is SOUN Worth Buying as AI Growth Clashes With Persistent Losses?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025860/is-soun-worth-buying-as-ai-growth-clashes-with-persistent-losses?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog_plus%7Czer_report_insights-3025860","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793983620.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"c